"{#} Hz, mostly mode {#} (free plate mode at {#} Hz; the driver's {#} g moving mass on the post shifts it). Detuned by +{#} Hz; width f/Q = {#} Hz. It is symmetric about both center lines and both diagonals.",
"The wave driver shakes the post. At low frequency the whole plate rides up and down with it, so where the plate's acceleration passes g everywhere all the sand hops, farther the lower the frequency. Near a resonance the plate bends far more than the post moves, and the sand settles on the nodal lines. The driver setting x₀ = {#} mm means a coil force of {#} N (see Model); Q = {#} gives each peak a width f/Q.",
